findings.why:
Service.request signs `{timestamp}
{method}
{path}
` + body with path being the relative path passed by callers (/v1/reviews and /v1/reviews/{id}). The test's verify uses the same relative path so it passes, but the server must re-derive the exact signed path. If the server signs the full request URI (including any trailing slash or query) or the URL is built with self.url.rstrip('/') + path, the two can disagree; more concretely, Service stores url possibly with a path prefix (e.g. https://host/api), and request() signs only `/v1/reviews` while sending https://host/api/v1/reviews — the HMAC is over a path the server cannot reconstruct from the request. Any deployment behind a path prefix is silently rejected with 401.
